17. what is const ?
    JavaScript variable declaration.
    const div = (
      <div>
        <button>Click Me</button>
        <p>paragraph of text {2 + 2}</p>
        {ChatInput()}
      </div>
    );

   <div>, <button>, and <p> — HTML-like markup written using JSX syntax.
   {2 + 2} — a JavaScript expression inside JSX, which evaluates to 4.
   {ChatInput()} — calls the JavaScript function ChatInput() and inserts its returned value into the JSX

   Important: JSX allows you to write HTML-like markup inside JavaScript. The browser cannot directly execute JSX; a
   tool such as Babel transforms it into JavaScript.

